<rml>
<head>
<style>
/*
	The live-reload gate fixture (VaCuus.Render.IdleGate.LiveReload, bead VaCuus-akj.6.42(b)).

	A FILE and not an inline string, because the door under test only opens for files:
	UVaCuusView::ReloadDocument() refuses a view whose DocumentPath is empty, and
	LoadDocumentFromMemory() clears that path on purpose (VaCuusView.cpp:188-191, :226-230).
	An inline document is not live-reloadable, so an inline fixture would test nothing.

	One opaque box, no text and no image: text would need a font face (a fontless element
	logs "No font face defined" per layout pass -- bead VaCuus-akj.21), and an image would
	put an async decode into a test that is about the reload. What is left is geometry, which
	is exactly what a reload has to release and re-compile.

	Static on purpose: no animation, no transition, no :hover. The test's first assertion is
	that the idle gate ARMS -- fewer publishes than recorded frames -- and anything that moved
	on its own would keep republishing and make the reload's publish unattributable.
*/
body { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
#box { display: block; position: absolute; left: 12px; top: 12px; width: 120px; height: 90px; background-color: #2050C0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div id="box"/>
</body>
</rml>
